  "changed_since_previous": "Replaced the previous approach of just connecting block peers last with connecting eviction candidates first and slowing tx and block peer ping responses, resolving netgroup sort discrepancies across standard library implementations; added assertions for `last_transaction` and `last_block` timestamps and explicit waits for `minping`.",
  "card": "Fixes a test gap in p2p_eviction.py where peer eviction tests passed even if block-time protection logic was disabled or peers never transmitted blocks. In the original test, fallback connection-age protection shielded the block peers, and platform-specific std::sort implementations in netgroup protection produced inconsistent peer selection. The test now connects eviction candidates first with faster pings than block and tx peers, and explicitly validates peer block and transaction timestamps. No dependencies.",
